# SABOTAGE: issue #46 — the test stops pinning the clock and falls through to
# `Crypto.fresh_timestamp?/2`'s real-wall-clock default on ONE call inside the
# deterministic boundary test. `pinned_now` is a fixed HISTORICAL epoch
# (1_700_000_000, Nov 2023); with the `now:` override dropped, that call reads
# the REAL current wall clock instead, which is now roughly two years further
# on — `abs(real_now - ts)` is on the order of tens of millions of seconds,
# nowhere near the 300s tolerance, so the `assert` (expecting "fresh") flips to
# a hard, deterministic failure. No timing race is needed to prove the pin
# matters: an unpinned call against a fixed historical timestamp fails every
# single time, by a huge margin, on every machine, forever.
#
# NOT TOUCHED: `Samen.Fleet.Crypto.fresh_timestamp?/3` itself (the seam this PR
# adds), the other pinned assertions in the same test, and every other test.
#
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/fleet_crypto_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: PINNED CLOCK: the exact boundary is deterministic
diff --git a/samen_core/test/fleet_crypto_test.exs b/samen_core/test/fleet_crypto_test.exs
index e560929..dd4ecb5 100644
--- a/samen_core/test/fleet_crypto_test.exs
+++ b/samen_core/test/fleet_crypto_test.exs
@@ -98,7 +98,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Fleet.CryptoTest do
       tolerance_s = 300
 
